  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Grant Aid in Response to the Earthquake in Western Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 7 October 2023, a 6.3 magnitude earthquake struck 40km west of Herat City in Herat Province, western Afghanistan. Several aftershocks have occurred since, with the initial quake felt in neighboring Badghis and Farah provinces. On 11 October, another earthquake of 6.3 magnitude struck 31km northwest of Herat and was followed by an aftershock of 5.0 magnitude. According to the latest Multi-Sectoral Rapid Assessment data as of 10 October, there are reportedly thousands of families affected with 1,394 recorded deaths, 13,373 injured, and hundreds of houses destroyed. These numbers will increase as information is compiled.Sanitation services have been identified as a priority need by the International Organization for Migration (IOM). Almost all households reported having no access to sanitation facilities due to destruction of their latrines, no education, lack of awareness about hygiene and cleanliness. To prevent a concurrent cholera outbreak and maintain the health and dignity of those affected, IOM is establishing toilets and shower facilities at both the household and camp level in a gender-sensitive manner, ensuring that IOM&#x2019;s sanitation interventions are universally accessible but also mindful and supportive of the specific needs and challenges encountered by various gender demographics.</narrative>
  </description>
